  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n\ufeff\ufeff\ufeff\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ 3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-(-1)(3) & =0 \\\\ 1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+3 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +4 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(1)(4)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{-12}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =1\\pm \\sqrt{3}\\text{i}.$",
